00:10:30,555 --> 00:10:31,629
the truck itself.

282
00:10:31,979 --> 00:10:34,219
So why did it fall faster?

283
00:10:34,399 --> 00:10:36,840
Because the Hummer was the most expensive

284
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:37,614
of the group,

285
00:10:37,614 --> 00:10:39,637
and it depended the most on buyers

286
00:10:39,637 --> 00:10:41,483
who did not need to count every

287
00:10:41,483 --> 00:10:41,899
dollar.

288
00:10:42,079 --> 00:10:44,074
Once the tax credit was gone,

289
00:10:44,074 --> 00:10:45,794
even those buyers waited.

290
00:10:45,974 --> 00:10:48,108
There is a lesson here for every

291
00:10:48,108 --> 00:10:50,108
truck, not just electric ones.

292
00:10:50,288 --> 00:10:51,763
The more a truck costs,

293
00:10:51,763 --> 00:10:53,817
the more its sales depend on the

294
00:10:53,817 --> 00:10:55,036
mood of the market.

295
00:10:55,216 --> 00:10:57,068
And in twenty twenty-six,

296
00:10:57,068 --> 00:10:58,328
the mood changed.

297
00:10:58,678 --> 00:11:01,208
Number five is the Tesla Cybertruck.

298
00:11:01,388 --> 00:11:03,713
It is the most famous electric truck

299
00:11:03,713 --> 00:11:05,973
on earth, and the numbers around it

300
00:11:05,973 --> 00:11:07,781
are the hardest to pin down,

301
00:11:07,781 --> 00:11:10,816
because Tesla does not report Cybertruck sales.

302
00:11:10,996 --> 00:11:12,621
So we use estimates,

303
00:11:12,621 --> 00:11:13,759
and we say so.

304
00:11:13,939 --> 00:11:15,767
According to InsideEVs,

305
00:11:15,767 --> 00:11:17,516
citing Cox Automotive,

306
00:11:17,516 --> 00:11:20,140
Tesla sold about twenty thousand,

307
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:23,637
two hundred Cybertrucks in the United States

308
00:11:23,637 --> 00:11:25,386
in twenty twenty-five.

309
00:11:25,566 --> 00:11:27,041
In twenty twenty-four,

310
00:11:27,041 --> 00:11:29,386
it sold about thirty-nine thousand.

311
00:11:29,736 --> 00:11:30,850
Estimates differ.

312
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:33,952
GM Authority put the twenty twenty-five total

313
00:11:33,952 --> 00:11:35,964
closer to twenty-five thousand.

314
00:11:36,144 --> 00:11:38,617
Either way, the direction is the same.

315
00:11:38,797 --> 00:11:41,202
And in the first quarter of twenty

316
00:11:41,202 --> 00:11:44,597
twenty-six, Cox Automotive data posted by Sawyer

317
00:11:44,597 --> 00:11:47,992
Merritt showed the Cybertruck at three thousand,

318
00:11:47,992 --> 00:11:49,548
five hundred nineteen,

319
00:11:49,548 --> 00:11:52,660
down forty-five percent from a year earlier.

320
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,826
That is still the top seller among

321
00:11:54,826 --> 00:11:56,578
electric pickups that quarter.

322
00:11:56,758 --> 00:11:59,746
The best-selling electric truck was selling less

323
00:11:59,746 --> 00:12:01,924
than four thousand in three months.

324
00:12:02,275 --> 00:12:03,540
Here is the twist.

325
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,971
In September of twenty twenty-five,

326
00:12:05,971 --> 00:12:08,608
Tesla dropped the cheapest version of the

327
00:12:08,608 --> 00:12:11,181
Cybertruck, the one that was supposed to

328
00:12:11,181 --> 00:12:12,532
bring the price down.

329
00:12:12,712 --> 00:12:14,166
According to Electrek,

330
00:12:14,166 --> 00:12:16,480
sales in the second quarter of that

331
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,529
year were around five thousand.

332
00:12:18,709 --> 00:12:20,723
The truck that was meant to be

333
00:12:20,723 --> 00:12:22,939
the future of the pickup became a

334
00:12:22,939 --> 00:12:25,558
niche product, loved by some owners and

335
00:12:25,558 --> 00:12:27,103
ignored by most buyers.

336
00:12:27,453 --> 00:12:29,194
One more note on honesty.

337
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:32,173
For the third quarter of twenty twenty-six,

338
00:12:32,173 --> 00:12:35,364
Pickup Truck Talk estimates about three thousand,

339
00:12:35,364 --> 00:12:38,228
seven hundred, and about eleven thousand for

340
00:12:38,228 --> 00:12:39,660
the first nine months.

341
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:42,611
The article itself calls that a low-confidence

342
00:12:42,611 --> 00:12:44,960
estimate based on the earlier run rate.

343
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:47,462
We include it because it points the

344
00:12:47,462 --> 00:12:49,320
same way as everything else.

345
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:50,915
But it is an estimate,

346
00:12:50,915 --> 00:12:52,716
not a reported sales number.

347
00:12:53,066 --> 00:12:55,481
Number six is the Rivian R1T,

348
00:12:55,481 --> 00:12:58,229
and its story is the quietest one

349
00:12:58,229 --> 00:12:59,312
on this list.

350
00:12:59,492 --> 00:13:00,918
Rivian is a startup,

351
00:13:00,918 --> 00:13:02,345
not a Detroit giant,

352
00:13:02,345 --> 00:13:04,556
and it was the first company to

353
00:13:04,556 --> 00:13:06,910
put an electric pickup on sale in

354
00:13:06,910 --> 00:13:07,410
volume.

355
00:13:07,590 --> 00:13:10,852
According to Cox Automotive data posted by

356
00:13:10,852 --> 00:13:14,115
Sawyer Merritt, the R1T sold one thousand,

357
00:13:14,115 --> 00:13:17,533
six hundred fifty-eight in the first quarter

358
00:13:17,533 --> 00:13:19,165
of twenty twenty-six,

359
00:13:19,165 --> 00:13:21,806
down just four percent from a year

360
00:13:21,806 --> 00:13:22,427
earlier.

361
00:13:22,778 --> 00:13:24,901
Four percent is a small fall,

362
00:13:24,901 --> 00:13:27,831
and next to the Cybertruck at forty-five

363
00:13:27,831 --> 00:13:30,834
percent and the Silverado EV at forty-one

364
00:13:30,834 --> 00:13:32,884
percent in the same quarter,

365
00:13:32,884 --> 00:13:34,422
it looks almost calm.

366
00:13:34,602 --> 00:13:37,033
The twist is that the smallest company

367
00:13:37,033 --> 00:13:37,865
held up best.

368
00:13:38,045 --> 00:13:39,621
The R1T is expensive,

369
00:13:39,621 --> 00:13:41,423
it is not aimed at work,

370
00:13:41,423 --> 00:13:43,750
and its buyers are not the same

371
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:45,777
people who buy a Silverado.

372
00:13:45,957 --> 00:13:47,574
That might be why it did not

373
00:13:47,574 --> 00:13:48,325
fall as hard.

374
00:13:48,505 --> 00:13:50,898
A smaller audience can be a steadier

375
00:13:50,898 --> 00:13:51,164
one.

376
00:13:51,514 --> 00:13:53,666
Number seven is not a truck that

377
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:54,137
failed.

378
00:13:54,317 --> 00:13:55,816
It is a truck that has not

379
00:13:55,816 --> 00:13:56,911
been delivered yet,

380
00:13:56,911 --> 00:13:58,870
and it might be the most important

381
00:13:58,870 --> 00:13:59,101
one.

382
00:13:59,281 --> 00:14:00,894
On June twenty-fourth,

383
00:14:00,894 --> 00:14:04,413
twenty twenty-six, Slate Auto revealed the price

384
00:14:04,413 --> 00:14:06,026
of its electric truck.

385
00:14:06,206 --> 00:14:08,654
It starts at twenty-four thousand,

386
00:14:08,654 --> 00:14:10,597
nine hundred fifty dollars,

387
00:14:10,597 --> 00:14:12,037
not including taxes,

388
00:14:12,037 --> 00:14:14,484
registration and destination fees.

389
00:14:14,664 --> 00:14:16,626
Preorders opened that same day.

390
00:14:16,976 --> 00:14:18,763
The truck is as simple as a

391
00:14:18,763 --> 00:14:20,087
modern truck can be.

392
00:14:20,267 --> 00:14:21,919
According to Electrek,

393
00:14:21,919 --> 00:14:25,074
it has a sixty-five kilowatt-hour battery,

394
00:14:25,074 --> 00:14:27,928
a rear motor of one hundred eighty-one

395
00:14:27,928 --> 00:14:31,007
horsepower, and an estimated range of two

396
00:14:31,007 --> 00:14:32,434
hundred five miles.

397
00:14:32,614 --> 00:14:35,168
It comes as a two-seat pickup that

398
00:14:35,168 --> 00:14:37,872
owners can turn into a five-seat SUV

399
00:14:37,872 --> 00:14:38,698
themselves.

400
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:41,056
It has no infotainment screen,

401
00:14:41,056 --> 00:14:42,872
and one gray body finish.

402
00:14:43,052 --> 00:14:45,808
Slate plans to sell wraps instead of

403
00:14:45,808 --> 00:14:46,268
paint.

404
00:14:46,618 --> 00:14:47,999
Now the twist.

405
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:50,935
Slate originally pitched the truck at under

406
00:14:50,935 --> 00:14:52,473
twenty thousand dollars,

407
00:14:52,473 --> 00:14:55,165
but that price assumed the seven thousand,

408
00:14:55,165 --> 00:14:57,665
five hundred dollar federal tax credit,

409
00:14:57,665 --> 00:14:59,139
which no longer exists.

410
00:14:59,319 --> 00:15:01,764
The company has raised about one point

411
00:15:01,764 --> 00:15:03,114
four billion dollars,

412
00:15:03,114 --> 00:15:05,173
and it plans to sell directly to

413
00:15:05,173 --> 00:15:07,167
customers, with no dealerships.

414
00:15:07,347 --> 00:15:10,470
First deliveries are still expected by the

415
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:12,328
end of twenty twenty-six.

416
00:15:12,508 --> 00:15:15,418
But Electrek notes that electric startups have

417
00:15:15,418 --> 00:15:18,328
often failed to deliver affordable vehicles at

418
00:15:18,328 --> 00:15:18,708
scale.

419
00:15:19,058 --> 00:15:20,163
Before the close,

420
00:15:20,163 --> 00:15:22,309
let's put the whole market on one

421
00:15:22,309 --> 00:15:25,171
table, because the pattern gets clearer when

422
00:15:25,171 --> 00:15:26,732
you see it side by side.

423
00:15:26,912 --> 00:15:29,559
Through the first nine months of twenty

424
00:15:29,559 --> 00:15:32,478
twenty-six, according to Pickup Truck Talk,

425
00:15:32,478 --> 00:15:35,873
the Chevrolet Silverado sold four hundred thirteen

426
00:15:35,873 --> 00:15:38,860
thousand, three hundred eighty-three trucks,

427
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,693
down less than one percent.

428
00:15:40,873 --> 00:15:43,687
The GMC Sierra sold two hundred fifty-two

429
00:15:43,687 --> 00:15:46,021
thousand, six hundred thirty-nine,

430
00:15:46,021 --> 00:15:46,364
flat.

431
00:15:46,544 --> 00:15:48,098
Even Ford's F-Series,

432
00:15:48,098 --> 00:15:50,243
down six point eight percent,

433
00:15:50,243 --> 00:15:52,907
still sold more than half a million.

434
00:15:53,257 --> 00:15:56,002
Now compare those numbers with the electric

435
00:15:56,002 --> 00:15:56,322
ones.

436
00:15:56,502 --> 00:15:59,536
The gas and diesel trucks barely moved,

437
00:15:59,536 --> 00:16:00,159
or grew.

438
00:16:00,339 --> 00:16:02,856
The electric trucks fell by forty,

439
00:16:02,856 --> 00:16:04,855
sixty, even ninety percent.

440
00:16:05,035 --> 00:16:06,951
That is the real twist of this

441
00:16:06,951 --> 00:16:07,717
whole story.

442
00:16:07,897 --> 00:16:10,219
The pickup truck market did not shrink.

443
00:16:10,399 --> 00:16:11,678
A small slice of it,

444
00:16:11,678 --> 00:16:13,789
the slice that was supposed to be

445
00:16:13,789 --> 00:16:16,667
the future, shrank while everything around it

446
00:16:16,667 --> 00:16:17,435
held steady.

447
00:16:17,615 --> 00:16:19,635
The buyers did not leave trucks.

448
00:16:19,815 --> 00:16:22,404
They left the electric version of trucks.

449
00:16:22,754 --> 00:16:23,868
Why does that matter?

450
00:16:24,048 --> 00:16:26,255
Because a truck buyer is a different

451
00:16:26,255 --> 00:16:27,113
kind of buyer.

452
00:16:27,293 --> 00:16:28,814
A truck is a tool.

453
00:16:28,994 --> 00:16:30,972
It tows a trailer on a Friday,

454
00:16:30,972 --> 00:16:32,751
hauls lumber on a Saturday,

455
00:16:32,751 --> 00:16:34,927
and sits in a driveway on Sunday.

456
00:16:35,107 --> 00:16:37,578
A buyer who does that cares about

457
00:16:37,578 --> 00:16:39,151
range with a trailer,

458
00:16:39,151 --> 00:16:40,873
charging on a job site,

459
00:16:40,873 --> 00:16:43,420
and what the truck costs per mile.

460
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,786
When the tax credit disappeared,

461
00:16:45,786 --> 00:16:48,862
the electric truck lost its biggest argument,

462
00:16:48,862 --> 00:16:50,229
which was the price.

463
00:16:50,579 --> 00:16:52,725
Look at what the carmakers chose to

464
00:16:52,725 --> 00:16:53,400
build next.

465
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:56,304
Ford is bringing back the Lightning with

466
00:16:56,304 --> 00:16:57,121
a generator.

467
00:16:57,301 --> 00:17:00,193
Ram is rebuilding the one thousand five

468
00:17:00,193 --> 00:17:02,343
hundred REV with a V six that

469
00:17:02,343 --> 00:17:04,197
only charges the battery.

470
00:17:04,377 --> 00:17:07,640
GM insiders are reportedly looking at plug-in

471
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:08,220
hybrids.

472
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,263
Three different companies,

473
00:17:10,263 --> 00:17:11,840
three different plans,

474
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:12,986
one shared idea.

475
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:14,673
Keep the electric drive,

476
00:17:14,673 --> 00:17:17,060
but add something that does not depend

477
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:18,379
on finding a charger.

478
00:17:18,729 --> 00:17:20,683
There is a cost to that change,

479
00:17:20,683 --> 00:17:21,945
and it is not small.

480
00:17:22,125 --> 00:17:24,679
Ford took a nineteen point five billion

481
00:17:24,679 --> 00:17:25,596
dollar charge.

482
00:17:25,776 --> 00:17:28,979
General Motors said earlier in twenty twenty-six

483
00:17:28,979 --> 00:17:31,582
it would lose about six billion dollars

484
00:17:31,582 --> 00:17:34,251
from repealing its electric investments.

485
00:17:34,431 --> 00:17:37,219
That is more than twenty-five billion dollars

486
00:17:37,219 --> 00:17:38,583
between two companies,

487
00:17:38,583 --> 00:17:40,132
spent changing direction.

488
00:17:40,312 --> 00:17:42,244
And that is only what the companies

489
00:17:42,244 --> 00:17:42,796
announced.

490
00:17:42,976 --> 00:17:45,735
The real cost includes the jobs paused

491
00:17:45,735 --> 00:17:48,349
at Factory Zero and the workers sent

492
00:17:48,349 --> 00:17:48,712
home.

493
00:17:49,062 --> 00:17:51,086
And what about the buyer who already

494
00:17:51,086 --> 00:17:51,593
owns one?

495
00:17:51,773 --> 00:17:53,171
This is a fair question,

496
00:17:53,171 --> 00:17:55,151
and it deserves a straight answer.

497
00:17:55,331 --> 00:17:57,801
A warranty normally stays valid on a

498
00:17:57,801 --> 00:18:01,025
discontinued model, and an electric truck still

499
00:18:01,025 --> 00:18:03,151
works the same on the day after

500
00:18:03,151 --> 00:18:04,317
the announcement.

501
00:18:04,497 --> 00:18:05,856
The risk is value.

502
00:18:06,036 --> 00:18:08,125
A truck with a famous name and

503
00:18:08,125 --> 00:18:10,842
no future often loses value faster than

504
00:18:10,842 --> 00:18:13,211
a truck that is still being built,

505
00:18:13,211 --> 00:18:15,927
so check resale numbers before you pay.

506
00:18:16,278 --> 00:18:18,400
So what is the pattern across all

507
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:18,785
seven?

508
00:18:18,965 --> 00:18:21,612
One electric truck was ended after a

509
00:18:21,612 --> 00:18:24,701
nineteen point five billion dollar charge.

510
00:18:24,881 --> 00:18:27,350
One was cancelled and came back as

511
00:18:27,350 --> 00:18:28,004
a hybrid.

512
00:18:28,184 --> 00:18:30,719
Two lost almost half their sales once

513
00:18:30,719 --> 00:18:32,363
the tax credit was gone.

514
00:18:32,543 --> 00:18:34,610
One lost sixty-two percent.

515
00:18:34,790 --> 00:18:37,143
One is a famous truck that sells

516
00:18:37,143 --> 00:18:38,393
in the thousands,

517
00:18:38,393 --> 00:18:40,305
not the tens of thousands.

518
00:18:40,485 --> 00:18:42,482
And one is still a promise.

519
00:18:42,662 --> 00:18:44,894
The lesson is not that electric trucks

520
00:18:44,894 --> 00:18:45,541
are doomed.

521
00:18:45,721 --> 00:18:47,665
It is that they were priced and

522
00:18:47,665 --> 00:18:49,860
planned for a world with a subsidy,

523
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:51,178
and that world ended.

524
00:18:51,528 --> 00:18:53,437
That matters if you are thinking about

525
00:18:53,437 --> 00:18:55,347
buying a truck in twenty twenty-seven.

526
00:18:55,527 --> 00:18:56,816
Here is what to check.

527
00:18:56,996 --> 00:18:59,613
First, find out whether the exact model

528
00:18:59,613 --> 00:19:01,022
is still being built,

529
00:19:01,022 --> 00:19:02,162
and for how long.

530
00:19:02,342 --> 00:19:05,522
A discontinued truck can lose value quickly,

531
00:19:05,522 --> 00:19:08,484
and parts and service attention can fade.

532
00:19:08,664 --> 00:19:10,993
Second, look at the sales trend of

533
00:19:10,993 --> 00:19:12,774
that model, not the brand.

534
00:19:12,954 --> 00:19:15,227
A truck that fell sixty percent in

535
00:19:15,227 --> 00:19:17,366
a year is telling you something.

536
00:19:17,716 --> 00:19:20,003
Third, ask what replaces it.

537
00:19:20,183 --> 00:19:22,558
Right now, the answer from Ford and

538
00:19:22,558 --> 00:19:24,594
Ram is a range-extended truck,

539
00:19:24,594 --> 00:19:26,766
and from GM it is still unclear.

540
00:19:26,946 --> 00:19:28,931
Fourth, count the full cost.

541
00:19:29,111 --> 00:19:32,480
Charging, fuel, insurance and what the truck

542
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:34,854
will be worth in five years all

543
00:19:34,854 --> 00:19:36,692
belong on the same page.

544
00:19:36,872 --> 00:19:39,194
And fifth, never buy a truck because

545
00:19:39,194 --> 00:19:41,063
of a promise about next year.

546
00:19:41,243 --> 00:19:43,007
Buy the truck that exists today,

547
00:19:43,007 --> 00:19:44,715
with the numbers you can check.

548
00:19:45,065 --> 00:19:46,625
We put all of this into a

549
00:19:46,625 --> 00:19:50,057
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

550
00:19:50,237 --> 00:19:52,246
It covers the numbers to check,

551
00:19:52,246 --> 00:19:54,189
the questions to ask a dealer,

552
00:19:54,189 --> 00:19:56,522
and the warning signs we just walked

553
00:19:56,522 --> 00:19:57,040
through.

554
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:59,257
The link is in the description and

555
00:19:59,257 --> 00:20:00,576
in the pinned comment.

556
00:20:00,756 --> 00:20:02,945
If you want to see which trucks

557
00:20:02,945 --> 00:20:05,418
keep disappearing from dealer lots,

558
00:20:05,418 --> 00:20:08,808
subscribe, because the next video covers exactly

559
00:20:08,808 --> 00:20:09,161
that.

560
00:20:09,341 --> 00:20:10,409
Thanks for watching.
